HST Office: Word's Borders and Shading. One dialog with Borders, Page Border and Shading tabs, opened by both
.uno:BorderDialog and .uno:BackgroundDialog. Selected text inside one paragraph starts on Apply to: Text.

- Page Border edits the current page style, with Word's Apply to: whole document, this section, first page only,
  all except first page. A section here is a page style, which is what a Word section becomes on import.
- w:pgBorders w:display now round-trips. Import ignored it and export always wrote allPages.
- Apply to Text writes the character border, shadow and background, so w:bdr and w:shd on the run in DOCX. The
  export dropped a direct w:bdr, taking the run's own border for an inherited one.
- SwDoc::ChgPageDesc copies the master's border to the first page format; it keeps the first page's own when
  the page style is marked for first page only or all except first page.

